{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1ozxwyi","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"group-15-elements-nitrogen-family","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pconcentrated-nitric-acid-upon-long-standing-turns-yello-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-qbiloqve4jutigfz","content":"<p>Concentrated nitric acid, upon long standing, turns yellow-brown due to the formation of</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"NO"},{"identifier":"B","content":"NO<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"N<sub>2</sub>O"},{"identifier":"D","content":"N<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>The reaction involved is 4HNO<sub>3</sub> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 4NO<sub>2</sub> + 2H<sub>2</sub>O + O<sub>2</sub>. The yellow-brown color appears due to the formation of NO<sub>2</sub>.</p>"}]}